course: dictionary
lesson: 7707
title: A word about the mind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Psychiatric is a long word, but its clues are in the words around it. «She works as a psychiatric nurse.» A nurse is a helper, and psychiatric tells you the nurse cares for illnesses of the mind.
explain: The dictionary says psychiatric means about psychiatry, the medical care of illnesses of the mind, such as serious depression or anxiety. Doctors who treat these illnesses are called psychiatrists. To check, swap in the words "illness of the mind": «a nurse for illnesses of the mind» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Old words can hide the truth. «Went away for a rest» is an old-fashioned phrase for spending time in a psychiatric hospital. People used it because they felt embarrassed. Today we use the true words, because mental illness is a real illness that doctors treat, just like a broken leg.
fact: Psychiatric means about the medical care of illnesses of the mind.
fact: A psychiatrist is a doctor who treats illnesses of the mind, such as serious depression or anxiety.
fact: «Psychiatric hospital» means a hospital for illnesses of the mind.
fact: «Psychiatric help» means medical help for mental health.
fact: Careless writers use psychiatric as an insult, but that is unkind, so always use it with respect.
exercise: «She trained to be a psychiatric nurse.» What does psychiatric describe? | Work with animals on a farm | *Care for illnesses of the mind | Work on a ship at sea | Work that is very fast
exercise: What is a psychiatrist? | A teacher who runs a school | *A doctor who treats illnesses of the mind | A shop worker who sells medicine | A doctor who fixes broken bones
exercise: «Went away for a rest» is an old-fashioned phrase. What does it mean? | *Spending time in a psychiatric hospital | Going for a walk in the park | Sleeping outside in a tent | Going on a long holiday abroad
test: Which phrase means a hospital for illnesses of the mind? | *Psychiatric hospital | Dental hospital | Heart hospital
test: Why is it kind to use psychiatric correctly? | *Because mental illness is a real illness that doctors treat | It makes a story scarier | It is a rude word for crazy
exam: Which sentence uses psychiatric respectfully? | He is so psychiatric, what a weirdo | *She works as a psychiatric nurse, caring for people with illnesses of the mind | The psychiatric dog ran off | Our psychiatric teacher is mad
